    // Climate 1, the subtropical south (Guangdong, Guangxi, Hainan, Hong Kong
    // and Macau): an industrial load with a morning plateau, a lunchtime dip,
    // an air-conditioning afternoon that peaks from 14:00 to 17:00 in summer
    // and an evening peak at 19:00 to 20:00 in winter. The months run from
    // the Spring Festival trough in February to the July and August peak.
    // Climate 2, the Guizhou plateau: milder summers and a winter heating
    // evening peak. The hourly shapes and the February trough are authoring
    // judgments on the system clock (all cities keep CST): no sourced hourly
    // load profile was found. The July and August monthly peak follows
    // Guangdong's record peaks of 148 and 149 GW on 9 and 10 July 2024 (S&P
    // Global Commodity Insights, 2024-07-12, "Heatwave, economic growth drive
    // southern China's peak power load to record high").
    climates: [
        (id: 1,
            shapes: [
                ("winter", [
                0.80, 0.76, 0.74, 0.73, 0.73, 0.75, 0.82, 0.92, 1.02, 1.08, 1.11, 1.08,
